    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰμῐ-ευτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for housekeeping, thrifty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.115
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>
			<i>economy, thrift</i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				1.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Rome,
				<i>belonging to the quaestor</i> or <i>quaestorship</i>,
			Lat. <i>quaestorius</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τ. ἐξουσία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					8.77
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἀρχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
					7.1.3
				</span></i>
			 (Susa, <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>, Epist. Artabani), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Mi.</u>
				16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ νόμοι οἱ τ</span>. ibid.;
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τ. νόμος</span> the law
				<i>concerning the treasury</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Publ.</u>
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
